    "text": "[4.3  Progressive coding]\ncan transmit a\nsample x ∼q(x) using approximately DKL(q(x) ∥p(x)) bits on average for any distributions p and\nq, for which only p is available to the receiver beforehand. When applied to x0 ∼q(x0), Algorithms 3and 4 transmit xT , . . . , x0 in sequence using a total expected codelength equal to Eq. (5). The receiver,\n\nat any time t, has the partial information xt fully available and can progressively estimate:\nx0   =  xt  √ 1            /√ ̄αt                        (15)                         ≈ˆx0    −",
