    "text": "[4.3  Progressive coding]\nTable 1 also shows the codelengths of our CIFAR10 models. The gap between train and test is at\nmost 0.03 bits per dimension, which is comparable to the gaps reported with other likelihood-based\nmodels and indicates that our diffusion model is not overfitting (see Appendix D for nearest neighbor\nvisualizations). Still, while our lossless codelengths are better than the large estimates reported for\nenergy based models and score matching using annealed importance sampling [11], they are not\ncompetitive with ot",
    "source_section": "4.3  Progressive coding",
    "title": "Unknown",
    "authors": [],
    "year": null,
    "chunk_index": 52
