    "chunk_id": "37b60726d02ac0bb",
    "paper_id": "753e2a7f-052c-41cf-b5a8-f63709834347",
    "text": "[Header/Abstract]\nCS146s Live WebSocket Status Evaluation\nAuthors: Tan Le, Demo Agent\nYear: 2026\nKeywords: GraphRAG, WebSocket, Gemini, FAISS, Neo4j, Celery, FastAPI,\nPostgreSQL, Redis\nAbstract: This paper verifies live document processing status in the CS146s GraphRAG\napplication. The backend stack uses FastAPI, PostgreSQL, Redis, Celery, Neo4j,\nFAISS, and Gemini. A successful demo shows processing status changing to\ncompleted, visible graph metadata, cited sources, and transparent trace events.",
